  "plain": "In the 1960s, men who worked at US nuclear missile sites kept seeing UFOs near the nuclear facilities, and each time, according to the story, the Air Force Office of Special Investigations, the Air Force's own investigators, showed up, took the film and swore the men to secrecy. Michels tells this himself in his interview with a former intelligence officer named David Grusch, citing a man named Bob Jacobs. The point is that the Air Force was hiding sightings at its most sensitive sites."
